for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<p class="note">This diagram groups setup and runtime observations across alternative experiments. Host callbacks and local MCP handlers share a process but have different roles. Internal rule matching is reference guidance.</p><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen allow and deny rule workflow steps"></div>'+walk)

reference=[('Allow is pre-approval', 'An allow list is not the available-tool inventory and does not constrain bypass mode. Unlisted calls can reach the mode or callback. Reads in the working directory may already qualify as safe built-in approvals, so a successful read alone does not prove a particular allow entry decided it.'), ('Bare, scoped and wildcard deny', 'Bare Write removal is verified separately. Scoped rules match commands or paths as written. The supplied slides and current docs describe wildcard denial as removal. In the pinned SDK MCP experiment, initialization still reports MCP names and actual calls receive permission denials. This lab verifies denied execution, not MCP definition removal. The global * form is reference syntax, not another live experiment.'), ('MCP literal-server patterns', 'Valid allow forms include mcp__classroom__* and mcp__classroom__read_*. The server segment must be literal; mcp__*__read_lesson is not a valid MCP allow pattern. The live experiment uses local classroom and archive servers, not external accounts.'), ('Path anchors and write coverage', 'The live path experiment uses Edit(./protected/**). Current SDK docs specify Edit(path) for Write and NotebookEdit too; Write(path) is not equivalent. A double slash marks an absolute path, such as Edit(//secrets/**), while one slash anchors at the rule source. These anchor examples are reference syntax, not tested filesystem targets.'), ('Project source and mock .env', 'Only project mode enables settingSources project and writes actual .claude/settings.json. Read(./.env) protects a disposable mock file. The application’s real .env is never served or placed in the agent working directory.'), ('Ask before a write', 'The supplied lesson suggests asking before git push. This application demonstrates the same ask-to-callback mechanism using a fixed local Write; no git push is performed or simulated. The callback is programmed classroom policy, not a human approval dialog.'), ('dontAsk has qualifications', 'Pair pre-approved reviewer tools with dontAsk to deny calls that would prompt. Safe built-in operations may still run. Explicitly choose tools or use bare denies when removal is required. SDK permission rules alone are not an operating-system sandbox.'), ('Evidence and API cost', 'The nine experiments use actual SDK queries with a $0.40 budget threshold per query, not a prepaid cap. Hooks, callback calls, initialization names, native feedback, MCP handlers and host file checks are observed evidence. Media, dependencies and real credentials remain excluded from Git.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 28 · Allow and deny rules\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson28-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson28-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson28-allow-deny-rules`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3128 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK permission rules](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for offline boundary, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 28 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
